message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: >-
  Biclustering-Driven Feature Engineering for Robust Cross-Platform
  Generalization in Transcriptomic Cancer Classification
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-13
authors:
  - family-names: Babichev
    given-names: Sergii
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Informatics, Jan Evangelista Purkyne University in Usti
      nad Labem, Pasteurova 15, 400 96 Usti nad Labem, Czech Republic;
      Department of Physics, Kherson State University, University str. 17,
      Kherson, 73008, Ukraine
    email: sergii.babichev@ujep.cz
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6797-1467"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis pipeline for transcriptomic cancer classification,
  including data preprocessing, Gene Ontology-based filtering, ensemble
  biclustering, SOTA consensus clustering, Random Forest and XGBoost
  modelling, external validation, and ablation analysis.
keywords:
  - ensemble biclustering
  - gene expression data analysis
  - feature selection and filtering
  - SOTA consensus clustering
  - Random Forest
  - XGBoost
  - external validation
  - transcriptomic cancer classification
license: MIT
